  <h1>Physical Product Design</h1>
  
  <p>
    This course is all about bringing your design ideas to life in physical form. You’ll learn the fundamentals of 2D and 3D modeling using professional CAD software, then spend much of your time in the shop turning those designs into real objects. At least half of the course is devoted to hands-on fabrication with 3D printers, laser cutters, and a variety of shop and hand tools. You’ll cut, measure, glue, and build using materials and tools like X-Acto knives, T-squares, and other essentials of the designer’s bench. We’ll work together in a collaborative studio environment that encourages experimentation, problem-solving, and creative exploration. Through a series of projects, you’ll gain confidence moving between digital design and physical making, developing both precision and imagination in your work.
  </p>
